      <h2>Infrastructure demands more than a maintenance spreadsheet.</h2>
      <p>Aging assets. Multi-decade lifespans. Federal funding cycles. Environmental and regulatory obligations. The complexity of infrastructure operations has outpaced every software tool built before Assetas.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="points">
      <li><h3>Aging asset backlog</h3><p>Roads, bridges, tunnels, dams, and utility systems degrade on a schedule no one controls. Without continuous condition assessment and AI-driven prioritization, every year of deferred maintenance compounds risk — and cost.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Capital planning without real data</h3><p>CIP decisions worth hundreds of millions are made using inspection reports that are months old, condition scores that were never standardized, and spreadsheets that no one fully trusts. There is a better way.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Fragmented data across systems</h3><p>GIS, ERP, document management, maintenance, inspection apps, and project management tools each hold pieces of the picture. Without integration, no one — owner, operator, or regulator — can see the full condition of a portfolio.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Distributed workforce and contractors</h3><p>Infrastructure projects span years and involve dozens of contractors, subcontractors, inspectors, and agency reviewers. Coordination without a shared platform means gaps in records, delays in approvals, and unresolved deficiencies.</p></li>
